{
  "dom_id": "step-q359072",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "What is the $\\text{GCF}$ of $12z$ and $8z?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $12$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,6,\\,12.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $8$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,4,\\,8.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $12$ and $8$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,4.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $4.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. Both $12z$ and $8z$ contain $z.$\n\nThus, the greatest common factor of $12z$ and $8z$ is $4z.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
